-- Indonesia deep-dive content (English). Indonesia's story has a similar
-- shape to Colombia and Argentina: a genuine, real-time clearance model
-- (not a data-reporting-only regime), where DJP approval via Coretax is
-- now a legal precondition for a valid invoice -- but layered on top of
-- a much older e-Faktur mandate (2014-2016) that was already close to
-- universal before Coretax existed. Live-researched against
-- vatcalc.com, fiscal-requirements.com, hanumaglobal.com, muc.co.id,
-- and DJP's own site (pajak.go.id). mandate_summary and timeline_intro
-- deliberately kept short (per the lesson of migration 355, which had to
-- trim six countries whose these fields crept to 150-190 words).









